---
description: Archived Phaser experiment conventions
globs:
  - "experiments/loot-drop/**"
---

- This rule applies only to the archived/reference Phaser experiment. It does not make Phaser
  the root production engine. Follow the established structure: `scenes/` (Boot -> Preload -> LootDrop,
  extending `BaseScene`), `objects/` (one class per game entity, extending
  Phaser containers/images), `systems/` (VfxSystem, CameraDirector,
  RevealDirector, AssetManager, SoundEventBus), `assets/` (generatedTextures,
  assetManifest, spriteKeys).
- Logical resolution is 1280x720 with `Scale.FIT`; author all coordinates in
  that space.
- Use tweens and particle emitters, not physics, for motion. Fire-and-forget
  effects must destroy themselves.
- Texture keys come from `spriteKeys.ts` (PROC/HF constants) or the
  `AssetManager` role resolvers. Never hardcode texture strings or file
  paths in scene code.
- Every texture must have a procedural fallback in `generatedTextures.ts`;
  the game must boot with zero binary assets present.
- Long-lived loops (bobs, pulses) must be removed in `destroy()`/shutdown;
  subscribe/unsubscribe bridge and settings listeners on scene
  create/shutdown to survive scene restarts.
- Camera motion goes through `CameraDirector`; reveal sequencing goes through
  `RevealDirector`; particle effects go through `VfxSystem`. Do not scatter
  raw `cameras.main.shake()` or ad-hoc emitters around the scene.
